course: dictionary
lesson: 3492
title: Far: distance, amount and so far
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Far is a small word with several jobs. Most often it means a long way away: «A boy in Vancouver looks out of the window at the far trees.» The trees are a long way off, so far tells you where they are.
explain: Far can also ask a question. «How far» asks what the distance is, so it is a question about how long a road, a walk or a journey is. If the sentence is asking for a distance, far is the word that does the asking.
explain: Far can mean very much, as in «far more» or «far fewer». «Because energy is lost at each step, there are always far fewer predators than plant-eaters.» Far fewer means a lot fewer, not a long distance. Check by swapping in «a lot»: a lot fewer predators still makes sense.
explain: «So far» means up to now. The meaning comes from the whole phrase, not from far on its own, so always read the words around it before you decide what far means.
fact: Far means a long way away, as in «the far trees» in the distance.
fact: «How far» asks what the distance is.
fact: Far can mean very much, as in «far more» and «far fewer».
fact: «So far» means up to now.
fact: Farther and further are both forms of far, and farthest and furthest are the biggest distances.
exercise: «A boy looks out of the window at the far trees.» What does far mean here? | *A long way away | Up to now | Very quickly | Very much
exercise: «How far is it to the station?» What does how far ask for? | *The distance | The name of the station | The time of day | The number of people
exercise: «There are always far fewer predators than plant-eaters.» What does far fewer mean? | A long way away from the plant-eaters | Exactly the same number | *A lot fewer
test: Ella has read ten pages so far. What does so far mean? | *Up to now | Very much | Far from home | A long way away
test: «The farther a planet is from the Sun, the longer its year.» What does farther mean here? | A smaller distance | Very much fewer | Very quickly | *A greater distance
exam: Jayden says that far always means a long way away. Is he right? | No, far means very quickly | Yes, but only in maths | Yes, far always means distance | *No, far can also mean very much, and so far means up to now
